Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Space toggles and Alt+Enter opens details on Quick
 Settings tiles

Keyboard-first shade design for Quick Settings tiles. Arrows keep
Compose focus traversal between tiles and Enter keeps the tile's click
(its dialog or details on dual-target tiles), with the existing
borderOnFocus focus ring. Added on a focused tile:

* Space toggles: the switch of a dual-target tile (Internet,
  Bluetooth...), else the tile's normal click.
* Alt+Enter, the design's Menu / Fn+Enter on keyboards without Fn
  (Q25), runs the tile's long-press action: details or settings.

The action runs on the first key-down and its repeats and key-up are
consumed, so the clickable never also clicks; any other modifier
leaves the key alone. Pure policy: qs/sable/SableTileKeys.java. The
tile's click lambda is only moved into a val so both paths share it.
